# Grok skills in Cursor

Ignore this rule unless the workspace contains `.grok/skills/`.

Grok App Builder lists those skills automatically. Cursor, Cloud Agents, and Grok Bot coding agents do not — unless they are also on a Cursor discovery path (this repo exposes them as `.cursor/skills` → `.grok/skills`).

Before UI work, **Read** the matching `SKILL.md` (and `references/` on demand). Do not restyle from memory or Paper skills alone.

## Before overlay / design work

If the task is DOM UI, game chrome (title, HUD, pause, game over, scores), Paper `code-to-design` / `design-to-code`, tokens, theme, CSS, or restyle:

1. Read `.grok/skills/design-ui/SKILL.md` first (same files as `.cursor/skills/design-ui`).
2. Load `design-ui/references/` as needed (`refined-ui`, `typography`, `surfaces`, `animations`).
3. Follow that doctrine. Do not invent a parallel visual system.

Also read:

- `.grok/skills/building-games/SKILL.md` for canvas / 3D / gameplay (both skills when a game has overlay chrome)
- `.grok/skills/controls/SKILL.md` before WASD / vehicle / flight
- `auth` / `neon` only when that project's `AGENTS.md` §0.5 says so

Do not call `imagine_*` unless those tools are actually listed.

## Paper handoff

Paper is the visual source of truth. Implement only the requested delta. Copy-only asks stay copy-only. Do not ship Paper-only chrome (device status bars, decorative stand-ins) into the app.
